WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.610
Speaker 1: Well, ladies and gentlemen, we
had primaries last night.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:11.419
And as expected, Wyoming Republican Congresswoman
Liz Cheney has been absolutely, brutally defeated

00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:14.200
in her Republican primary.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.699
Did she abandon Republican orthodoxy?

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:23.230
Was she pro-choice or against lowering taxes
on the rich or any policy?

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.300
No, it wasn't anything like that.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:34.350
She simply said that Donald Trump really did
lose the election in 2020 and for that the

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.950
MAGA people determined that she had to be
punished and she will now be replaced on the

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:45.870
November final general election ballot by
Harriet Hagaman, an individual whose political

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.980
views are essentially identical to Liz Cheney's.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:55.430
With the exception that Harriet Hagaman has
parroted the claim that Joe Biden didn't really

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.170
win in November of 2020.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.960
And that apparently was a mortal sin.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.800
Let's talk about last night's primaries.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.140
As the Associated Press reports, Trump Fired
Cheney Loses Wyoming GOP Primary Ponders 2024

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.140
Bid.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.790
I don't even care about the 2024 thing for
now.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.440
She was on with Savannah Guthrie this morning
and sort of said, I'm going to think about

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.930
24.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.540
There's no real need to talk about that right
now.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.159
A lot of things will happen between now and
then.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:29.710
Liz Cheney, Trump's fiercest Republican adversary,
writes The AP in Congress soundly lost a Republican

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.280
primary, failing but falling to a rival backed
by the former president in a rout that reinforced

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.190
his grip on the party's base.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:42.880
The third term congresswoman and her allies
entered Tuesday downbeat about her prospects.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:43.880
And listen, she lost.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.961
I mean, I don't even really know what else
we need to pull from this.

00:01:46.961 --> 00:01:50.650
She lost and she lost very, very significantly.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:57.210
And the reason that she became a target of
the MAGA people and of Donald Trump is that

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:02.240
she insisted Trump didn't win in 2020.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.210
Trump really genuinely lost.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.220
She's still a Republican.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.470
She still voted the way Trump wanted.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:14.420
93% of the time when she was in Congress and
Trump was president.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.420
But she says no.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.430
Trump genuinely did lose.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:24.090
And in her concession speech, sort of her
or her speech that she gave, she says, I easily

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.430
won last time.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.090
I could have won again.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:31.180
I just would have had to lie and say that
Trump won and I wasn't willing to do that.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.569
Let's listen to what she had to say last night.

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:38.120
Speaker 2: Two years ago, I won this primary
with 73% of the vote.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.120
Speaker 1: True.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.300
Speaker 2: I could easily have done the same
again.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:48.090
The path was clear, but it would have required
that I go along with President Trump's lie

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.400
about the 2020 election.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.219
It would have required that I enable his ongoing
efforts to unravel our democratic system and

00:02:56.219 --> 00:02:59.280
attack the foundations of our Republic.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.420
That was a path I could not and would not
take.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:10.579
Speaker 1: The Lincoln Project commented on
Liz Cheney's primary loss.

00:03:10.579 --> 00:03:15.079
That's a group made of sort of non-Trump Republicans
for the most part.

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:18.469
And they said tonight marks the end of the
Republican Party.

00:03:18.469 --> 00:03:22.950
What remains share is the name of the Republican
Party.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:28.969
But it is, in fact, an authoritarian nationalist
cult dedicated only to Donald Trump.

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:31.859
So there's really two sides to this.

00:03:31.859 --> 00:03:37.499
Is it wacky and is it disturbing that this
is what the Republican Party has become?

00:03:37.499 --> 00:03:38.499
Of course it is.

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:39.840
Of course, it's wacky and disturbing.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.439
The goal of the MAGA people is to purge the
Republican Party of the critics of Donald

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:49.980
Trump, even something as benign as saying
the results were the real results Joe Biden

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.030
did when Donald Trump did lose.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.200
You've got Adam Kinzinger retiring.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.060
Liz Cheney lost her primary.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.330
Some of the other Republicans who did vote
to convict Trump on that second impeachment

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.489
trial are either retiring or lost primaries.

00:04:02.489 --> 00:04:08.129
So it is absolutely crazy that that's the
situation at the same time.

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:15.319
It's important to remind you that Liz Cheney
mostly voted with Trump and she's being replaced

00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:20.209
by someone who will mostly vote in the way
that Trump would want will vote with the Republican

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:21.209
Party.

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:22.209
Whatever.

00:04:22.209 --> 00:04:26.229
Harriet Hagaman will vote the same way as
Liz Cheney on just about every issue.

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:30.889
The only difference is Hagaman is willing
to repeat the big lie.

00:04:30.889 --> 00:04:32.720
Whereas Liz Cheney was not so.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:39.330
It's also disturbing because on policy there
is essentially no difference between Hagaman

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.400
and Cheney.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.150
They're both against abortion.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.590
They're both for, you know, lower taxes for
the rich, whatever.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:50.150
The difference is actually just one about
this issue where it's about an election that

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.490
was almost two years ago.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.770
So that's also sad.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.800
Now, these results could potentially backfire.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.599
And I'll mention the way in which that could
happen.

00:04:58.599 --> 00:05:00.849
Wyoming's total population is 580,000.

00:05:00.849 --> 00:05:04.770
No, I'm not saying 580,000 people voted yesterday.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.389
I'm not saying that's 580,000 Republicans.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:11.310
The total population of Wyoming is 580,000.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:18.870
Tiny electorate much more subject to having
a primary manipulated by out-of-state money

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.150
and Trump and the MAGA people.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.720
These results could send a signal to the more
reasonable Republicans in other parts of the

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.180
country to the extent that they exist and
to a little extent they do that the Republican

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:36.040
Party is now the MAGA Party, and many Republicans
aren't at all in favor of this being a MAGA

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.040
Party.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.569
If you're Mitt Romney, for example, it is
at this point, thanks to the Democratic Party,

00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:45.629
that we still even have some semblance of
democracy in the United States.

00:05:45.629 --> 00:05:50.360
But if you're Romney, you should understand
that your own party will come for you, at

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.280
least potentially.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.509
And we have to see what the impact is of that
on to the extent that they exist.

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:59.410
The more moderate and reasonable Republicans.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.950
Now, couple other elections from last night.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:09.669
Lisa murkowski also was challenged by a pro-Trump
Republican in Alaska in the Senate.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:15.500
She won enough votes to advance to the general
election in November in that Senate race.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:20.909
And Sarah Palin, although she did not get
the most votes in her Alaska congressional

00:06:20.909 --> 00:06:23.280
primary yesterday.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.770
She also will advance to November.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.009
So that's what's going on.

00:06:28.009 --> 00:06:29.690
And we're going to have these.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.830
It's an open House seat for Sarah Palin.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.699
And we will see in November what happens with
that.

00:06:33.699 --> 00:06:36.619
But very disturbing results, that's for sure

